2026-11-07T17:14:47.1278091Z === store-closing-fair.test.ts ===
2026-11-07T17:14:47.5604020Z 
2026-11-07T17:14:47.5604558Z The rules
2026-11-07T17:14:47.5608370Z   ok    the unused part is the payment times the share of its period after the closing day, rounded
2026-11-07T17:14:47.5609356Z   ok    nothing for a period that ends by the closing day, or for nothing paid
2026-11-07T17:14:47.5610080Z   ok    never more than the payment, even for a period that starts after the day
2026-11-07T17:14:47.5611013Z   ok    what was refunded already is taken off, never below nothing
2026-11-07T17:14:47.5611929Z   ok    a hold pauses collection with its invoices voided and no day to resume, and keeps a member's own pause
2026-11-07T17:14:47.5613514Z   ok    a release resumes collection, or puts a member's own pause back with its own day
2026-11-07T17:14:47.5615439Z   ok    the fixed sentence says the access comes from the store and the notice is at least seven days
2026-11-07T17:14:47.5616757Z   ok    a paid store's cap is two years of its plan's orders, a trial's is its orders
2026-11-07T17:14:47.5617196Z 
2026-11-07T17:14:47.5617753Z A store whose plan ends: held, told, ended and settled
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6211053Z   ok    on the day the plan ends every member is held, before the first notice goes out
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6211989Z   ok    the member's own pause is kept to be put back
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6218053Z   ok    and their last payments are written down
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6221397Z   ok    the first notice says members are not charged, buyers will be told, the refund that will be made and that a new plan keeps the store
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6223041Z   ok    it names the exact last moment, in UTC, as the studio and the checkout count it, and no longer says a plan can be started until the day itself
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6512627Z   ok    between the plan's end and the closing no member is charged
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6513675Z   ok    the creator is told three times, the buyers once, at least seven days before
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6514506Z   ok    every buyer and member is told, once each
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6520867Z   ok    the closing day is at least seven days after the last buyer was told
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6522922Z   ok    a member's notice says their payments stopped and what they will be refunded, from Marktmorgen with its address, in text and in HTML
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6524389Z   ok    no refund is made before the closing day
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6529772Z   ok    the review lists each member who paid past the day, with the proportional amount
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6538182Z   ok    a screen drawn before something changed refunds nothing
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6563969Z   ok    pressed twice, each member is refunded once, the proportional amount, from the creator's own account
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6653969Z   ok    on its day the store closes
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6654999Z   ok    every membership ends at once, none left running
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6655907Z   ok    and the closing day refunds nobody twice
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6656638Z   ok    what it kept for the closing is let go
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6657408Z   ok    and nobody is charged after it either
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6657809Z 
2026-11-07T17:14:47.6658416Z On the closing day, what the creator did not refund is refunded for them, once
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7100932Z   ok    nothing is refunded before the day
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7154752Z   ok    on the day, each member's proportional part is refunded, once, and the one already refunded is not
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7163761Z   ok    a refund twice is impossible: the next day refunds nothing
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7164335Z 
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7165065Z A balance that does not cover a refund: never made, the member told
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7412349Z   ok    no refund is made and nothing is owed by Marktmorgen
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7413484Z   ok    the member is emailed that it could not be made, with the creator's published contact and never their sign-in address
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7414634Z   ok    and the store still closes that day
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7415295Z 
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7416540Z A plan started again before the closing: as it was, nothing charged for the days between, nobody refunded
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7631411Z   ok    its members are let go
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7632206Z   ok    a member's own pause is put back with its own day
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7633415Z   ok    nothing is charged for the days between: voided while held, and no invoice is collected for them
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7634513Z   ok    every buyer told it closes is told it stays, once
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7635388Z   ok    nobody is refunded
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7635911Z   ok    and it leaves the line
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7636252Z 
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7637102Z A hold that fails is tried again every day; the notices go anyway, with the count, and the store closes on its day
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7693441Z   ok    the first notice goes on the first day, saying how many are not paused yet
2026-11-07T17:14:47.7695312Z   ok    the next day only the failure is tried again, and the one Stripe accepts is held
2026-11-07T17:14:47.8081219Z   ok    one that never pauses does not keep the store from closing on its day, where it ends with the rest
2026-11-07T17:14:47.8082515Z   ok    the member Stripe never let us pause is not told its payments stopped: it may be charged until the day
2026-11-07T17:14:47.8083057Z 
2026-11-07T17:14:47.8083604Z More than fifty pages of members: read a part a day, from where the last run stopped
2026-11-07T17:14:48.5979614Z   ok    the first run reads fifty pages and waits; the next reads the rest and the notice goes
2026-11-07T17:14:48.5991057Z 
2026-11-07T17:14:48.5991631Z An invoice issued before the hold is voided, never collected during it
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6052327Z   ok    its open invoice is voided at the hold, and Stripe's retries never charge it
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6052699Z 
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6053151Z The closing's calls to Stripe are capped before they are made; members past it are counted, never silent
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6091118Z   ok    only what the budget covers is called, and the member past it is counted in the notice
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6231598Z   ok    the member past the budget is still told the store closes, like the one held
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6233074Z   ok    the held member is told its payments stopped; the one past the budget, still charged, is told the truth instead
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6233923Z 
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6235455Z A refund the balance did not cover is tried again when the creator adds funds; only the closing day makes it final
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6309284Z   ok    a press that cannot refund takes only the two calls it made, from the budget, never the reserve
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6310960Z   ok    pressed without the funds: nothing refunded, and the member is still listed to try again
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6317518Z   ok    pressed again after the funds came: refunded once
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6318632Z   ok    the button's words say it can be tried again, not that it is final
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6319217Z 
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6319850Z A balance in another currency than the sale: weighed in the currency it settles in
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6389244Z   ok    a euro balance a little short of the refund in euros: nothing refunded
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6405583Z   ok    enough euros: refunded in the sale's currency, the proportional amount
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6406138Z 
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6406624Z Out of time: the refunds stop and say what is left, never pretend it is done
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6451984Z   ok    with no time left, nothing is refunded and the row is counted as left
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6453188Z   ok    the route sets its own maxDuration and a time budget below it
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6453533Z 
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6453934Z Once its memberships ended at Stripe, a store closes: starting a plan does not bring it back
2026-11-07T17:14:48.6651088Z   ok    the day began: its membership ended, the store not removed yet
